      "side": 1,
      "message": "This would be an issue if the user terminates the loop before reaching the end because then slab_unlock will not be called. Another bad case if user changes the page in the middle of the loop.\nA cleaner interface IMO would be smth like this:\n\nstruct track_iter {\n    struct page *page;\n    int pos;\n};\n\nstruct track_iter iter;\nstruct track *t;\n\nstart_track_iter(page, \u0026iter); // sets iter fields, slab_lock(page)\nwhile ((t \u003d get_track(iter)) !\u003d NULL) // gets the track, increments pos\n    print(t);\nend_track_iter(\u0026iter); // slab_unlock(page)",
      "range": {
