      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, that\u0027s an issue. Since module would be needing access to each track structure i was thinking about adding an iterator on top of this function, that\u0027ll resolve the above two issues that you mentioned.\n\nSomething like this in mm/slab.h , \n\n    #define for_each_object_track(__s, __p, __object,  __iter, __track, __alloc) \\\n\t for (__object \u003d get_track_object(__s, __p, __iter, __track, __alloc); \\\n                 __object !\u003d NULL; \\\n                 __iter +\u003d 1, __object \u003d get_track_object(__s, __p, __iter, \n                 __track, __alloc))\n\nand module will use this macro \"for_each_object_track\" instead of directly using above function. Let me know if this looks fine for you.\n\nThanks.",
